{
  "id": "2026-09-14-suggestions-content-attributes",
  "scope": "suggestions",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "question": "How should optional SuggestionPlugin presentation reach the content root while generic Editor skins remain independent?",
  "model": "GPT-6 / Codex; exact model variant unavailable",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2",
  "trigger": "The user rejected suggestion-specific selectors in generic Editor skins, requested a strict Plate UI skill repair, and asked whether plugin content attributes belong in core. Continuing implementation authorization covers the bounded repair.",
  "requirements": [
    "Generic live/static Editor skins contain no optional feature imports, selectors, classes, data-attribute knowledge or presentation branches.",
    "The existing SuggestionPlugin owns feature behavior; copied SuggestionKit owns colors and other visual values.",
    "Apply attributes to the existing content root without a presentation-only div, companion plugin, assembly prop forwarding, new subscription or competing event/ref owner.",
    "Preserve live/static behavior, inferred plugin configuration, explicit content-prop precedence, disabled/null configuration and editOnly.render policy.",
    "Preserve authored authority and previously established suggestion behavior; this correction does not certify the broader Google Docs parity audit."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reused the prior entrypoint ownership decision and the existing suggestion browser journeys. Rechecked all nearby attribute/render owners and generic Editor consumers, then ran focused core and registry tests, source typechecks, public type contracts, all 11 Chromium suggestion journeys, and fresh prototype/production construction and SSR probes. The earlier choice to place feature CSS in generic Editor skins was unrecorded and contradicted existing law; it is reversed here. Prior broad Google audit limitations remain unchanged.",
  "summary": "Pursue plugin-owned render.contentAttributes and remove optional-feature knowledge from generic Editor skins.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-13-suggestions-entrypoint-review",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "alternatives": [
    "Maximum-value cut: remove all optional presentation from generic Editor skins and delete the style-only SuggestionSurface wrapper. Retain the existing SuggestionPlugin because it owns a proven independent behavior job; put copied visual values on that plugin.",
    "Reuse render.attributes or render.useViewElementAttributes: rejected for this job because they target document nodes/keyed elements, not the exact content root.",
    "Use decorate.attributes alone or change retained rendering: ordinary range attributes do not reach every retained fragment; altering retained rendering creates another presentation path where existing semantic markers already suffice.",
    "Retain wrapContent: valid for structure/providers/interaction boundaries, but a div solely carrying feature selectors has no independent job.",
    "Forward props from EditorKit into generic Editor, add a companion plugin, broad HTML prop bag, dynamic hook host or imperative effect: rejected because each adds plumbing or competing ownership without satisfying an additional current requirement.",
    "Adopt safe static render.contentAttributes on the existing base plugin: Plate compiles editable/read-only snapshots once in the existing plugin publication path, and live/static content components merge them onto their existing roots. Plite already accepts DOM props and needs no feature-specific change."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "155 focused core tests, 17 registry tests, root/React-core/static source typechecks, public type contracts, targeted lint, registry generation and all 11 local Chromium journeys pass. The six 1/10/100-plugin by 1/1000-node prototype and production cohorts pass a fixed max(1ms,10%) p50 overhead budget; SSR/construction on a noisy shared host is a bounded cost guard, not a speedup or browser/native performance claim. Zero additional scans/subscriptions are source-inferred. Full www TypeScript stops at Footnote TS2769 line 389; an in-memory compiler-host control removing both new BasePlugin declarations reproduces the identical diagnostic. Native/mobile/assistive behavior, remote collaboration and complete Google Docs parity were not assessed.",
